            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there a plan to add this to every sensor daemon?  I feel like this should be solicited for feedback on the ML since it is a pervasive change to sensors."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Good point. sent the RFC to the ML."
                },
                {
                    "file": "/COMMIT_MSG",
                    "line": 7,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. https://lists.ozlabs.org/pipermail/openbmc/2025-December/037800.html"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Is this supposed to be atomically updated alongwith Value?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "In theory yes. But I need to check if we have support for this in PDI. Alternatively, I am thinking Value then ValueUpdatedTime is the least disruptive (User thinking a value is older than reality is probably less risky than a value being newer)."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 42,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Done. updated the description on when its recommended to be updated."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Should we set any flags? Readonly?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes. thanks for the suggestion. It should be marked read-only."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 43,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "What does this indicate?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 44,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "I changed it to infinity which will allow bmcweb to detect it as \"unsupported\" and leave it out of the Redfish data. Also updated the description to be more descriptive of what the default means."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Deepak Kodihalli",
                        "email": "deepak.kodihalli.83@gmail.com",
                        "username": "dkodihal"
                    },
                    "message": "Updated to D-Bus or updated in, say, cache/memory of a sensor service?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Thanks for the comment, I can make the description more clear that its the dbus property Value's last updated time."
                },
                {
                    "file": "yaml/xyz/openbmc_project/Sensor/Value.interface.yaml",
                    "line": 46,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Amithash Prasad",
                        "email": "amithash@meta.com",
                        "username": "amithash"
                    },
                    "message": "Done"
                }
